<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov rubber imports down 8.5 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov rubber imports down 8.5 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in November totalled 52,998 tonnes, down by 8.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Nov 96	 Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		52,998	 69,922	57,938</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   36,301	 50,705	41,748</p>
<p> Indonesia	  12,365	 13,957	10,318</p>
<p> Malaysia	    3,063	  3,951	 4,024</p>
<p>Imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 661,273 tonnes, against 629,729 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3-3432-7431)</p>
</text>
